Fix partial nested entity bug; add centralized exception handling

- Add RepositoryLookup.resolveOrThrow(), a generic helper that
  resolves a @ManyToOne reference to its full entity or throws
- Fix Book, Note, Quote, ListEntry, ContributorRelationship, and
  BookRelationship to resolve nested references before saving,
  rather than persisting/returning partial objects built from
  request JSON (only an id populated)
- Add EntityNotFoundException (404) for referenced ids that don't
  exist, and InvalidRequestException (400) for missing required
  references or invalid input
- Add GlobalExceptionHandler (@RestControllerAdvice) to translate
  both into clean JSON error responses instead of raw stack traces;
  also handles malformed request bodies (bad UUIDs, invalid enums)
- Require a book on Note, Quote, ListEntry, and ReadingEntry;
  require a book and contributor on ContributorRelationship
- Reject self-referential BookRelationship rows (bookA == bookB)
- Move ReadingEntry's book validation/resolution before the save,
  so it applies to every entry, not just completed+rated ones
